WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.050
Since 2017, Philadelphia has
taxed sweetened drinks at 1.5

2
00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.150
cents for every ounce.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.420
The city collects it from distributors.

4
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.840
Shoppers never send in a cent.

5
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:14.120
But sellers can raise their prices.

6
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.950
And buyers can decide
whether to keep buying.

7
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.330
So when a tax is charged to sellers,

8
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.700
who really ends up paying it?

9
00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:25.040
In this mission, you'll shift
the supply curve by the tax

10
00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.590
and shade the part each side carries.

11
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.970
Then you'll make a
prediction in a graph lab,

12
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.250
move a slider, and test it.

13
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:35.630
Your mission: find out
who really pays the tax.
